  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Nigerian Economic Summit Group</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this grant is to strengthen the research capacity of the Nigeria Economic Summit Group (NESG) in order to enhance evidence-based policy advocacy as well as to improve private sector participation in policy formulation, implementation, and monitoring in Nigeria. The NESG is an independent, non-partisan organization formed in 1995 that fosters open and continuous dialogue on the short, medium and long-term direction of Nigeria&apos;s economic policy and development between private and public sector leaders. The IDF funded program will seek to strengthen the NESG&apos;S capacity to carry out evidence-based research through building the capacity of a research faculty, training and development of the NESG research staff and creation of an online databank.  To strengthen the research capacity of the NESG in order to enhance evidence-based policy advocacy as well as to improve private sector participation in policy formulation, implementation, and monitoring.</narrative>
  </description>
